<%# The static hero content: an image cover, else a server-rendered thumbnail of the cover file,
    else the empty placeholder. Reused as the resting poster behind the 3D viewer. Reads the
    @cover_att / @model / @covers / @page_nodes ivars set by Models::Page (ModelsController#show).

    BOTH LIVE BRANCHES ASK ABOUT LIVENESS, AND THE SECOND ONE IS THE EASY MISS. @cover_att comes out
    of the already-partitioned @attachments, so the image branch is covered by construction; the
    thumb branch reads @model.cover_node_id, which is a raw column NOTHING validates against a live
    node (see ProjectsController#project_params for why that is deliberate). Unguarded it rendered a
    poll cell for a tombstone — /files/thumbnails omits a node with no row, so thumbs_controller's
    `if (!entry) continue` runs 40 times and the spinner never resolves. The empty placeholder is
    the honest answer. %>
<%# `inline_image?` ON THE NODE'S NAME, NOT THE ATTACHMENT'S ROLE (tinkerex#285): a .heic cover is
    an image by role and a broken picture as raw bytes; the thumb branch below shows it. The node
    comes from @page_nodes, the same live map the elsif reads, so a dead cover still falls through. %>
<% if @cover_att && Maker::FileAttachment.inline_image?(@page_nodes[@model.cover_node_id]&.name.to_s) %>
  <%= image_tag blob_file_path(@model.cover_node_id), class: "model-hero-img", alt: @model.title %>
<%# THE RENDER IS THE CARD, INK ON PAPER (UX audit 2026-11-01, E7; design-system rule 5). The cell
    is a plain wrapper and the `.thumb` inside it the card: it used to wear `.thumb` itself, painted
    `--raised` by pages/models.css, which outranked the component's `--thumb-stage` under the
    multiply blend, so in Graphite a render's white ground went the panel's dark colour.

    NO PICTURE COMING, NO EMPTY CARD (E3): when the cover's render has finished without one (an
    unsupported format, a failed render) and the model has a file the 3D viewer opens, a big blank
    card above "View in 3D" said nothing, so one line says it instead. A render still in flight keeps
    its card and spinner, because a picture is on its way. %>
<% elsif @page_nodes.key?(@model.cover_node_id) %>
  <% cover_thumb = @covers.thumb(@model.cover_node_id) %>
  <% if @viewable_3d.present? && cover_thumb && !cover_thumb.showable? && !cover_thumb.in_flight? %>
    <p class="model-hero-note muted">There is no preview picture for this model. <strong>View in 3D</strong> shows it.</p>
  <% else %>
    <span class="file-cell model-hero-thumb"
          data-controller="thumbs" data-thumbs-url-value="<%= thumbnails_files_path %>"
          data-thumbs-target="cell" data-node-id="<%= @model.cover_node_id %>" data-ext="">
      <%= render "files/thumb", thumb: cover_thumb, ext_label: "", url: preview_src(cover_thumb) %>
    </span>
  <% end %>
<% else %>
  <span class="model-hero-empty" aria-hidden="true"><%= rail_icon(:models) %></span>
<% end %>
